From: WhaleOS <whaleos-dev@navercorp.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gbm_mesa: import/map spoofed-format buffer in its R8 2D shape

Copyright (c) 2026 NAVER Corp.  All rights reserved.
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
See files/LICENSE.wrapper in this ebuild directory for the full text.


The gbm_mesa backend cannot allocate multi-planar YUV formats (NV12,
NV21, FLEX_YCbCr_420_888 etc.) through mesa's libgbm directly, so
gbm_mesa_bo_create() spoofs them onto a 4096-wide R8 2D texture:

    alloc_args.drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_R8;
    alloc_args.width  = bo->meta.total_size;
    alloc_args.height = 1;
    /* then: */
    alloc_args.height = DIV_ROUND_UP(width, 4096);
    alloc_args.width  = 4096;

The allocator-side process therefore ends up with libgbm holding the
buffer as a 4096 x ceil(total_size/4096) R8 2D texture, and
priv->map_stride is saved as 4096.

When the same buffer is later imported into a different process (e.g.
the 32-bit external camera HAL) the original gbm_mesa_bo_import() code
reverts the spoofing to "total_size x 1" and uses the client-view
stride (e.g. NV12 width).  mesa-libgbm then sees a 1D buffer view,
gbm_bo_map() returns NULL, and the camera HAL receives y=cb=cr=0x0
from lockYCbCr.  The matching gbm_mesa_bo_map() spoofed path has the
same defect: even when libgbm did manage to import a 2D R8 texture,
the map call asks for a region wider than its row stride and fails.
Finally, when the camera HAL allocates a JPEG output BLOB without
BO_USE_SW_MASK, gbm_mesa_bo_import() skips the libgbm import entirely;
later gbm_mesa_bo_map() then hits an unconditional
`assert(priv->gbm_bo != nullptr)` and aborts the camera service.

This patch makes three matching changes so the spoofed-format
invariants stay consistent across alloc / import / map / lazy-map:

  * gbm_mesa_bo_import(): for the spoofed format case, recompute
    s_width = 4096 / s_height = ceil(total_size/4096), save the R8
    stride into priv->map_stride, and hand libgbm the R8 stride (not
    the client-view stride) so it correctly interprets the buffer as
    a 2D R8 texture.

  * gbm_mesa_bo_map(): if priv->gbm_bo is still nullptr (the import
    skipped libgbm because BO_USE_SW_MASK was clear), do the libgbm
    import now using the same R8 2D reshape, and return MAP_FAILED if
    that import itself fails instead of asserting.  Then, when
    priv->map_stride > 0, ask libgbm to map the texture using that
    stride and the height derived from total_size so the region stays
    inside the texture.

With these three changes, lockYCbCr() in callers like
mapper@4.0-impl.minigbm_gbm_mesa returns valid y/cb/cr pointers and
the external camera HAL is able to convert V4L2 frames into Surface
buffers for the camera preview path.  The JPEG/BLOB path no longer
crashes the camera service either, although libgbm's PRIME-fd import
of a 4096-wide R8 texture still fails for some BLOB sizes, so JPEG
capture remains broken at the createJpegLocked level (downgraded from
SIGABRT to a clean "createJpegLocked failed" error that the HAL
reports back to cameraserver).  The non-spoofed (mesa-libgbm native
format) path is unchanged.

--- a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
+++ b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
@@ -416,15 +416,37 @@ int gbm_mesa_bo_import(struct bo *bo, struct drv_import_fd_data *data)
 		uint32_t s_format = data->format;
 		int s_height = data->height;
 		int s_width = data->width;
-		if (wr->get_gbm_format(s_format) == 0) {
-			s_width = bo->meta.total_size;
-			s_height = 1;
+		bool spoofed_fmt = (wr->get_gbm_format(s_format) == 0);
+		if (spoofed_fmt) {
+			/*
+			 * WhaleOS: align with the alloc-time spoofed-format
+			 * reshape in gbm_mesa_bo_create() that turns the buffer
+			 * into a 4096-wide R8 2D texture.  Importing as
+			 * total_size x 1 (the upstream behaviour) leaves libgbm
+			 * with a 1D view that gbm_bo_map() then refuses to
+			 * expose, so callers like the external camera HAL see
+			 * y=cb=cr=0x0 on lockYCbCr.  Use the same 4096 x
+			 * ceil(size/4096) shape that the allocator side used,
+			 * and save the R8 stride into priv->map_stride so the
+			 * bo_map fallback can pick it up.
+			 */
+			const uint32_t R8_TEX_WIDTH = 4096;
+			s_width = R8_TEX_WIDTH;
+			s_height = (bo->meta.total_size + R8_TEX_WIDTH - 1) / R8_TEX_WIDTH;
 			s_format = DRM_FORMAT_R8;
+			priv->map_stride = R8_TEX_WIDTH;
 		}

 		priv->drv = drv;
+		/*
+		 * For the spoofed path we must hand libgbm the R8 stride
+		 * (== s_width) too; data->strides[0] carries the original
+		 * client-view stride (e.g. NV12 width) and would make
+		 * mesa-libgbm misinterpret the underlying R8 texture.
+		 */
+		uint32_t import_stride = spoofed_fmt ? s_width : data->strides[0];
 		priv->gbm_bo = wr->import(drv->gbm_dev, data->fds[0], s_width, s_height,
-					  data->strides[0], data->format_modifier, s_format);
+					  import_stride, data->format_modifier, s_format);
 	}

 	bo->priv = priv;
@@ -456,7 +478,40 @@ void *gbm_mesa_bo_map(struct bo *bo, struct vma *vma, size_t plane, uint32_t map
 	vma->length = bo->meta.total_size;

 	auto priv = (GbmMesaBoPriv *)bo->priv;
-	assert(priv->gbm_bo != nullptr);
+
+	/*
+	 * WhaleOS lazy SW import: if the buffer was imported without
+	 * BO_USE_SW_MASK (e.g. JPEG output BLOB created by the camera HAL),
+	 * priv->gbm_bo is nullptr and the upstream code would assert.
+	 * Import it into libgbm now, applying the same 4096-wide R8 2D
+	 * reshape that gbm_mesa_bo_create / gbm_mesa_bo_import use for any
+	 * format libgbm does not understand natively.  This keeps the
+	 * spoofed-format invariants consistent across alloc / import / map.
+	 */
+	if (priv->gbm_bo == nullptr) {
+		int fd = priv->fds[0].Get();
+		if (fd < 0)
+			return MAP_FAILED;
+
+		uint32_t i_width  = bo->meta.width;
+		uint32_t i_height = bo->meta.height;
+		uint32_t i_stride = bo->meta.strides[0];
+		uint32_t i_format = bo->meta.format;
+		if (wr->get_gbm_format(i_format) == 0) {
+			const uint32_t R8_TEX_WIDTH = 4096;
+			i_width  = R8_TEX_WIDTH;
+			i_height = (bo->meta.total_size + R8_TEX_WIDTH - 1) / R8_TEX_WIDTH;
+			i_stride = R8_TEX_WIDTH;
+			i_format = DRM_FORMAT_R8;
+			priv->map_stride = R8_TEX_WIDTH;
+		}
+
+		priv->drv = drv;
+		priv->gbm_bo = wr->import(drv->gbm_dev, fd, i_width, i_height,
+					  i_stride, bo->meta.format_modifier, i_format);
+		if (priv->gbm_bo == nullptr)
+			return MAP_FAILED;
+	}

 	void *buf = MAP_FAILED;

@@ -464,8 +519,28 @@ void *gbm_mesa_bo_map(struct bo *bo, struct vma *vma, size_t plane, uint32_t map
 	int s_width = bo->meta.width;
 	int s_height = bo->meta.height;
 	if (wr->get_gbm_format(s_format) == 0) {
-		s_width = bo->meta.total_size;
-		s_height = 1;
+		/*
+		 * WhaleOS fix for the gbm_mesa spoofed-format path: the
+		 * underlying gbm_bo was allocated as an R8 2D texture with
+		 * actual dimensions priv->map_stride x ceil(total_size /
+		 * map_stride) (see the "Allocate 1D buffer as %dx%d R8 2D
+		 * texture" log path in gbm_mesa_bo_create()).  The original
+		 * code asks libgbm to map total_size x 1, which exceeds the
+		 * texture's row stride and gbm_bo_map() returns NULL --
+		 * camera HAL then sees y=cb=cr=0x0 on lockYCbCr.
+		 *
+		 * Use the saved map_stride and derive an integer height that
+		 * is large enough to cover total_size, so libgbm can map the
+		 * texture in its native shape.
+		 */
+		if (priv->map_stride > 0) {
+			s_width = priv->map_stride;
+			s_height = (bo->meta.total_size + priv->map_stride - 1) /
+				   priv->map_stride;
+		} else {
+			s_width = bo->meta.total_size;
+			s_height = 1;
+		}
 	}

 	wr->map(priv->gbm_bo, s_width, s_height, &buf, &vma->priv);
